Right — then do not add [disabled] to opti-checkbox. Since mat-option itself supports [disabled], we can use that to prevent selection, and the TS guard ensures the checkbox event cannot accidentally select an inactive Location.

1. search-autocomplete.component.html

Use this:

<ng-container *ngIf="filteredOptions | async as options">
  <mat-option
    *ngFor="let option of options"
    [value]="option"
    [disabled]="isOptionDisabled(option)"
    class="custom-option"
  >
    <opti-checkbox
      [checked]="isSelected(option)"
      (click)="$event.stopPropagation()"
      (checkboxChange)="toggleSelection(option)"
      [noFormGroup]="true"
      [title]="
        searchPlaceholder() === AddPanelType.BillingGroup
          ? option.name + ' (' + option.id + ')'
          : option.name
      "
    >
    </opti-checkbox>
  </mat-option>
</ng-container>

Notice that opti-checkbox has no [disabled].


